<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48565" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tormĭna</span></b> , um,
		n. (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>masc.</i> collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tormĭnes</span></b> , acc. to <i><span class="en">Non.
				32, 11</span></i>) [torqueo], <i>a griping of the
				bowels</i>, <i>the gripes</i>, <i>colic.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: proxima his, inter intestinorum mala,
			tormina esse consueverunt: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσεντερία</span> Graece vocatur, etc., <i><span class="en">Cels. 4,
			15</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 156, 5</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">157, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc. 2, 19, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 6, 7,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 22, 25, 72, § 148</span></i>; <i><span class="en">26, 8, 47, §
			74</span></i>; <i><span class="en">29, 5, 33,
				§ 103 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tormina urinae,</span>”
				<i>strangury</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					20, 8, 30, § 74</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">30, 15, 50,
				§ 144</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
